{"title": "Attitude", "pageid": 20777, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Attitude", "categories": ["Gameplay mechanics"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote noexcerpt\">Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/Approval\" title=\"Approval\">Approval</a>        </div>\n\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Trader_attitude.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/95/Trader_attitude.jpg/300px-Trader_attitude.jpg.webp, /w/images/9/95/Trader_attitude.jpg 1.5x\"><img alt=\"The meter displaying a trader's Attitude. Hovering over the meter displays the exact amount of Attitude gained.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/95/Trader_attitude.jpg/300px-Trader_attitude.jpg.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"181\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/95/Trader_attitude.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption><div class=\"noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable\">  The meter displaying a trader's Attitude. Hovering on the meter displays the exact amount of Attitude gained.  </div></figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Attitude</b> is used to determine the favourability (or lack thereof) of otherwise non-aggressive <a href=\"/wiki/Non-player_characters\" title=\"Non-player characters\">Non-Player Characters</a> and the prices they accept when trading. Attacking a character, stealing, or interacting with objects without permission may cause a nearby character who can be traded with (i.e. merchant or trader) to lose attitude towards the offending character. The only way to increase attitude is to gift gold or items of value.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Maximizing_trader_attitude\">Maximizing trader attitude</span></h2>\n<p>It can be a good idea to maximize the attitude of certain traders as early in the game as possible, especially if they reappear in later acts and offer expensive items. \n</p><p>For a more in-depth description of the effects of attitude on trading, see the page: <a href=\"/wiki/Trading_and_item_pricing\" title=\"Trading and item pricing\">Trading and item pricing</a>.\n</p><p>The best way to improve trader attitude seems to be gifting coins rather than items. This is because gifting an item is equivalent to gifting that item's <i>current</i> sell price. If an attitude of 100 is reached by gifting coins, and then those items are sold instead of gifted, the net cost for the trading party member (gold gifted - all items subsequently sold) is lower than simply selling items to obtain the same attitude of 100.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<ul><li>Attitude is trade specific and does not generally reflect a non-player character's opinion (i.e., <a href=\"/wiki/Approval\" title=\"Approval\">approval</a>) of the active character, unless sufficiently negative. In this case, the given NPC will not converse with the offending character unless remedied with a gift of enough value to bring their attitude sufficiently positive again.</li>\n<li>If an offense is committed by a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mage_Hand\" title=\"Mage Hand\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f9/Mage_Hand_Icon.webp/20px-Mage_Hand_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f9/Mage_Hand_Icon.webp/30px-Mage_Hand_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f9/Mage_Hand_Icon.webp/40px-Mage_Hand_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Mage Hand\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f9/Mage_Hand_Icon.webp/20px-Mage_Hand_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f9/Mage_Hand_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mage_Hand\" title=\"Mage Hand\">Mage Hand</a> or <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Find_Familiar\" title=\"Find Familiar\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8b/Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp/20px-Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8b/Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp/30px-Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8b/Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp/40px-Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Familiar\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8b/Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp/20px-Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8b/Find_Familiar_Cat_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Find_Familiar\" title=\"Find Familiar\">Familiar</a>, then the Mage Hand or Familiar takes the attitude loss instead.</li>\n<li>If the trading party member is <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Disguise_Self\" title=\"Disguise Self\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8d/Disguise_Self_Icon.webp/20px-Disguise_Self_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8d/Disguise_Self_Icon.webp/30px-Disguise_Self_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8d/Disguise_Self_Icon.webp/40px-Disguise_Self_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"disguised\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8d/Disguise_Self_Icon.webp/20px-Disguise_Self_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8d/Disguise_Self_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Disguise_Self\" title=\"Disguise Self\">disguised</a> when attitude changes happen, those changes only affect that specific disguise - not the character as a whole.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"navbox-styles\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r138587\">.mw-parser-output